{"title":"2007 BMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Albania</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/9576e51c7703b7fb9d7b9e3878732659e4253bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=BC=CD$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afdbc404e9f5f6880e249536724abc80c595e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\neq BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection point of its diagonals. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e3be9d4f79b0471fdd7556ad73e97a23eb6eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=DE$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd77ee064061e2405beb4f2ebfab979ab1bdfdaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD+\\angle ADC = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb71d5ba363a314c0343efdd9a19aafe8070c75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c836ab43a12add12f0863dfaad1e23ab29ad1b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\angle ACB$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />, and similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/2/77208f17e35af61db9d911a3d4dc1aa3b7d2f6c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBD = \\angle BDC$\" width=\"138\" height=\"12\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9d2e0b0b913f1c7bfae8007238206b5127d3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CEB = \\angle AED$\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" />, by considering triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/256cebaa0f7341af4ec4e2ba93143c098a8adcad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CEB, AED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1ab9cd9693f48d7b5cba3b50f6feae7436014b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC + \\angle BDC = \\angle ECB + \\angle CBE = \\angle EAD + \\angle EDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"453\" height=\"14\" />.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e410bbbe7c8c9137d47dc703f793ff5fa3f7b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 ( \\angle BAC + \\angle BDC ) = \\angle BAD + \\angle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"317\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c2eeca7e1fa3df5d4b8c8d8213c966b8506721e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AE}{DE} = \\frac{AE}{EB} \\cdot \\frac{EB}{EC} \\cdot \\frac{EC}{DE} = \\frac{\\sin (\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta)}{\\sin \\alpha} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\alpha}{\\sin \\beta} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\beta}{\\sin (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha)} = \\frac{\\sin (\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta)}{\\sin (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"682\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee00ae7bb3b4286a04aa16717bbafae7a6bbd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5ddf5002ceb158aa03c8bb509114b9f1f228efc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta) = \\sin (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9047b28aa73c3a8649109e495005978bb74a9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\alpha, \\beta &lt; \\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/1316ab62513fdc1d1efe0447b00bb009c900e03c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; (\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta) + (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha) &lt; 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />,\n</center>\n<p>and\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93da4b1ff91cea97dfd30ea7ef9472f62f689bd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\pi &lt; (\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta) - (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha) &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"309\" height=\"18\" />.\n</center>\n<p>From these inequalities, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/388ea5d083786550130542f598e3661560c4cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta ) = \\sin (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd57b655d177cdc6ede1fe6d9c9a0acb48c3ca86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta) = (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"226\" height=\"18\" /> (i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb20e93132e1900f67863ab0cdbdb41e11be1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54ca74a71a0b7704894d43bff4d6265214fee77b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pi - 2\\alpha - \\beta) + (\\pi - 2\\beta - \\alpha) = \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" /> (i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bbc91f1bc6d56565cff0cdaf155830307f64f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(\\alpha + \\beta) = \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />).  But if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb20e93132e1900f67863ab0cdbdb41e11be1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, then triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dddacd2a652126458c23cf6cacdcc9ea6fab1fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC, BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> are congruent and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775d96c2f45a2f26ea9709c286148883f1bde82a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = BD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />, a contradiction.  Thus we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee00ae7bb3b4286a04aa16717bbafae7a6bbd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/9487a52055282e672501e7c58ab06e50e4e9aa68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta = \\pi/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />, Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e8d2ac669e5d38483f32f67f01b7c4447d97a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;BAC = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e925d1005f2c7032300569190376e74864dd9b6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;BDC = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />. Then by the isosceles triangles manifest in the figure we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/5561620357a3b34509effecb03558fc237e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;DBC = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1bcaf0f691d145ad8c7f7bee1a550464000abe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;ACB = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/062d72136c0dd4e865a4e2e5d0148c25c261b467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;BEA = x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107ebf3be5feef0d8bf350dff621ff707f3e1bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;EAD = &lt;EDA = \\frac{x+y}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"217\" height=\"37\" />. Furthermore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/2176d832f4516e86f275b5977d5265912456cb6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;AEB = 180^\\circ - 2x - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d5d475fd06298de53f0b033b55cc2b231d00c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;DCE = 180^\\circ - x - 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee00ae7bb3b4286a04aa16717bbafae7a6bbd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a377cb8eb25001f379fccacb05e33fcbbe0ffc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE \\neq CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />. But also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a427387ff6212e24b2c3bf3ce692b2e62d50a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = CD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />, so by SSA \"Incongruence\" (aka. the Law of Sines: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07c4f2ee8d870beda95b8e281cd512719d06b8a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AE}{\\sin &lt;ABE} = \\frac{AB}{\\sin &lt;BEA} = \\frac{CD}{\\sin &lt;CED} = \\frac{DE}{\\sin &lt;ECD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"447\" height=\"38\" />) we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54edd808130309c77f038f6b3b258e014289f742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;ABE + &lt;DCE = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"202\" height=\"14\" />. This translates into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0dbb82bedbcb97b87a5fb2366d2650e05b780999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ = 3x + 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce2f13b223eead66d6777d0d6b27a3f3ee28ea47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ = 2x + 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />, which incidentally equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7cef9b98570c29c4b4466cb92068bba9505e591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;BAD + &lt;ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f0f8c9c000bb9f13e72d449bfc21091b6a20b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;BAD + &lt;ADC = 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"202\" height=\"14\" />, then also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356cf999c65e18acf08fbd93a7de06c2a10f5869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + &lt;EAD + &lt;EDA = x + y + (x + y) = 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"408\" height=\"18\" /> by the Exterior Angle Theorem, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70ae35cc283cbf51da78d821892d8d013825c5c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 3y = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f832877745d1f6b08280cfb47981f7d8eece14be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/755961ff4ab1f7a2e51a31fb43bc1f2a91307737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;DCE$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> are supplementary. A simple Law of Sines calculation then gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee00ae7bb3b4286a04aa16717bbafae7a6bbd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />, as desired. This completes both directions of the proof.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems\" title=\"2007 BMO Problems\">2007 BMO Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=827187#827187\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213643\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 274/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 344/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9998/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.332      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.332      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4910:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213643 and revision id 63347. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}